    "problem_statement": "JSONStorage ignores custom json.dumps kwargs\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using JSONStorage with custom kwargs for json.dumps (like `sort_keys`, `indent`, etc.), the kwargs are being ignored and not passed to the json.dumps call.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom tinydb import TinyDB\nimport tempfile\nimport os\n\n# Create a temporary database file\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', delete=False, suffix='.json') as f:\n    db_path = f.name\n\ntry:\n    # Initialize TinyDB with custom JSON formatting\n    db = TinyDB(db_path, sort_keys=True, indent=4, separators=(',', ': '))\n    db.insert({'b': 1})\n    db.insert({'a': 1})\n    db.close()\n    \n    # Read the file content\n    with open(db_path, 'r') as f:\n        content = f.read()\n    \n    print(\"Actual output:\")\n    print(repr(content))\n    print(\"\\nExpected formatted JSON with indentation and sorted keys\")\n    \nfinally:\n    os.unlink(db_path)\n```\n\nThe database file should contain properly formatted JSON with sorted keys and indentation, but instead it contains minified JSON without the custom formatting."
  },
